Report: Either branch operations and conditional callback composition
26 claims; 0 removal(s).
  run_ids: ["1f8874a4-834a-4220-9e19-263f87b1ebc5"] -> ["169c47a8-db98-4f5f-b8e9-7020b5df293e"]
  title: "Branch operations, borrowed views and payload factoring in Either" -> "Either branch operations and conditional callback composition"
  explanation: "For either 1.19.0 with default features on x86_64, is_left/is_right identify the actual branch; left/right return the corresponding optional payload; left_or/right_or select that payload or the given default; flip swaps the branch and a separate composition theorem proves flipping twice returns the original value. left_and/right_and select the supplied value or preserve the opposite payload. factor_none moves the optional payload outside Either while retaining its tag. factor_first/factor_second move the common tuple component outside Either. as_ref preserves the variant and referenced value; as_mut preserves the initial view and its generated backward function writes a matching-variant replacement payload back to the original variant. The fourteen original bodies terminate normally in the model for all well-typed values in their stated domains." -> "Twelve callback APIs compose a supplied mathematical callback contract with variant selection. is_left_and/right_and apply the callback only to the indicated variant and otherwise return false; is_left_or/right_or return true on the indicated variant and apply the callback to the other. map_left/right map only the named payload and preserve the other variant and payload. map_left_or/right_or return the mapped named payload or the supplied default. left_or_else/right_or_else preserve the named payload or compute it from the opposite payload. left_and_then/right_and_then return the selected callback-produced Either unchanged, or preserve the opposite variant and payload. Their normal-result proofs explicitly assume the supplied FnOnce dictionary returns the mathematical function value on every argument. Separate companion theorems show selected callback failure is propagated unchanged and non-selected branches preserve their result without any callback success premise. For either 1.19.0 with default features on x86_64, the following value-semantic guarantees exclude payload destructor effects; they do not establish Rust panic freedom for arbitrary Drop implementations. In that model, is_left/is_right identify the actual branch; left/right return the corresponding optional payload; left_or/right_or select that payload or the given default; flip swaps the branch and a separate composition theorem proves flipping twice returns the original value. left_and/right_and select the supplied value or preserve the opposite payload. factor_none moves the optional payload outside Either while retaining its tag. factor_first/factor_second move the common tuple component outside Either. as_ref preserves the variant and referenced value; as_mut preserves the initial view and its generated backward function writes a matching-variant replacement payload back to the original variant. The twenty-six original bodies terminate normally in the model for all well-typed values in their stated domains."
  trusted_assumptions: "The Rust compiler, official Charon/Aeneas translation, standard-library models and Lean kernel are trusted. Transitive theorem axioms are limited to propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. No local helper contracts or custom models are assumed. Reference contracts use Aeneas's value and backward-function semantics; they do not independently verify the compiler borrow checker or Rust aliasing model." -> "The Rust compiler, official Charon/Aeneas translation, standard-library models and Lean kernel are trusted. Transitive theorem axioms are limited to propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. No additional axioms or custom models are assumed; callback behavior is an explicit premise of the conditional composition theorems. Reference contracts use Aeneas's value and backward-function semantics; they do not independently verify the compiler borrow checker or Rust aliasing model."
  environment: "Original crates.io either 1.19.0 Rust files and Cargo.toml, archive-compared; default features, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. Rust nightly-2026-09-17, Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f, Aeneas be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a, Lean 4.35.0. The union of the fourteen roots is extracted once into one Generated module and proved in one Proofs module." -> "Original crates.io either 1.19.0 Rust files and Cargo.toml, archive-compared; default features, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. Rust nightly-2026-09-17, Charon 08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f, Aeneas be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a, Lean 4.35.0. The union of the twenty-six roots is extracted once into one Generated module and proved in one Proofs module."
  evidence_url: "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/bfd99993002c959e3581f36a16497af7a25606fb" -> "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/4f097e0e57af4422b08b2362fc92a1babff70dca"
  limitations: "Only the fourteen named methods and the two-flip composition are proved. Remaining inherent methods, callback-taking APIs, iterators, pinning, standard trait implementations and serde remain unproved. Rust destructor behavior and resource consumption are outside the pure value model. All-feature/no-default configurations and other targets were not proved." -> "Callback termination, panic freedom, captured-state effects and concrete closure correctness are not established by these conditional composition proofs. The theorem hypotheses describe modeled FnOnce results; unchanged modeled failure propagation does not specify Rust panic payloads, unwinding or external effects. Only the twenty-six named methods and the two-flip composition are proved. Other inherent and callback-taking APIs, iterators, pinning, standard trait implementations and serde remain unproved. Rust destructor behavior and resource consumption are outside the pure value model. All-feature/no-default configurations and other targets were not proved."
